Polygon offset as dynamic state (D3D12_OPTIONS16.DynamicDepthBiasSupported + ID3D12GraphicsCommandList9::RSSetDepthBias).
The PSO key held the raw float bits of POLY_OFFSET_SCALE/BIAS (KZ3 patch 2006) and D3D12 baked them into the PSO, so a
title that changes its shadow bias every frame built (and the walker awaited) new PSOs every frame: ToD Fastoon,
tods-play-1140, 1,132 PSOs over frames 2559-2815 from 18 new shaders, 42 s of creates, ~1 s walk per frame. Now, when the
device supports it, an offset-on PSO carries D3D12_PIPELINE_STATE_FLAG_DYNAMIC_DEPTH_BIAS and only "offset on" in its key
(rsx_dyn_bias.h), and the draw passes the values (as 2006 baked them) to RSSetDepthBias. Otherwise, or with LD_NO_DYN_BIAS=1,
everything is as before. The pipeline stream path gets a FLAGS subobject. LD_PSO_KEYLOG lines gain the raw offset words.
Log: "[caps] list9=.. dynamic-depth-bias=..". Host test: R&C port/rc/tests/run_dyn_bias_test.sh.
Rebased onto v0.18.0 + KZ3 2c5081a5, 2026-11-02: unchanged; it applies with a 3-way merge only (line offsets). Checked
that the render-state hash (ld_hash_structural_render_state, KZ3 2141 era) is still fed from ld_pso_key_tail's local
copy that ld_dynb_key_bits rewrites, so the key carries "offset on" only.

